   "hash_note": "Dataverse publishes the md5 of the ORIGINAL csv (e858ae14...) but the plain access endpoint serves the converted .tab (f2feb5ac...). Both were downloaded and both hashes reproduced on 2026-10-28; the membership rule was read from the .tab."
  },
  "factor_and_key": {
   "source": "Goldberg, L. R. (1992). The development of markers for the Big-Five factor structure. Psychological Assessment, 4(1), 26-42. Table 3.",
   "doi": "10.1037/1040-3590.4.1.26",
   "pdf_url": "https://projects.ori.org/lrg/PDFs_papers/Goldberg.Big-Five-Markers-Psych.Assess.1992.pdf",
   "pdf_note": "scanned, APA copyright. The PDF is NOT redistributed here - only the term->factor mapping (facts, not expression). The local copy was 2,600,352 B / 17 pages.",
   "extraction": "pdftoppm -r 300 -gray | tesseract --psm 4 on the two pages carrying Table 3 (printed pp. 34-35 = PDF pages 9-10)",
   "rule": "the OCR renders the key glyphs unreliably (I+, I__., -, II-- , N, V_), so the key is taken POSITIONALLY: within each Factor block the first key header is \"+\", the second is \"-\". A \"(continued)\" header does not reset that counter.",
   "match": "100/100 OCR term rows matched a TDA BFFM100 spelling exactly; 0 extra, 0 missing"
  },
  "independent_shape_check": {
   "source": "psychTools::BFI.adjectives.dictionary keying (personality-project.org docs), same Goldberg 1992 set",
   "finding": "its Neuroticism key lists 14 positive-keyed and 6 negative-keyed items; Table 3 Factor IV (Emotional Stability, opposite polarity) is 6 (+) / 14 (-). The two agree.",
   "note": "the other four factors are 10/10 in both."
  }
 },
